#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""perihelion-theme: color the desktop with Catppuccin, matched to the wallpaper.

Reads the wallpaper, picks a Catppuccin flavor (Latte, Frappé, Macchiato or
Mocha) from how light it is, and three Catppuccin accents from its strongest
colors. Then writes them everywhere the shell draws:

  ~/.config/simpbar/matugen.json        the bar, the cava wave, desktop widgets
  ~/.config/nwg-drawer/drawer.css       the app drawer (Super+A)
  ~/.config/fuzzel/fuzzel.ini [colors]  the launcher and the power menu
  ~/.config/strata/themes/tokyo-night.toml   Strata, the file manager
  ~/.config/mango/colors.conf           Mango's window borders

and tells simpbar and simpbar-shell to reload (SIGUSR1). Every color is a
real Catppuccin color: nothing is invented from the image, only chosen.

Settings, ~/.config/simpbar/theme (Simpbar Config writes it):
  flavor=auto        auto (from the wallpaper), latte, frappe, macchiato, mocha
  accent=wallpaper   wallpaper (picked from the image) or flavor (blue, pink,
                     yellow: Perihelion's look)

A file you edited by hand is left alone: the drawer CSS, fuzzel colors and
Strata theme are only rewritten while they still hold Perihelion's defaults
or this script's own output. Turning off "Catppuccin theme" in Simpbar
Config (auto_theme "manual") stops all of it.

Usage:
  perihelion-theme                 theme from the current wallpaper
  perihelion-theme IMAGE           theme from IMAGE
  perihelion-theme --color '#RRGGBB'
  options: --flavor F  --accent wallpaper|flavor  --force  --dry-run (print
           the chosen palette as JSON, write nothing)
"""

